.TH CYAML_STR_VAL 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cyaml_str_val \- extract a string value from a CYAML_STRING node
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cyaml.h>

const char *cyaml_str_val(cyaml node);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Returns a read-only pointer to the null-terminated string that node
stores.  The function calls _ccol_fatal_err() when node is NULL and
when node is not of type CYAML_STRING.

The node owns the string, so the caller must not free the pointer.
It is borrowed and stays valid until the node gets a new value or is
destroyed, so any of these ends it: a cyaml_set(3) that reaches the
node, a cyaml_list_remove(3), cyaml_dictionary_remove(3) or
cyaml_delete(3) of the node, a cyaml_dictionary_set(3) that replaces
it, and a destroy of its tree.  Copy the text if you need it longer.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
node  A CYAML_STRING node.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the node's own string buffer.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cyaml_type (3),
.BR cyaml_create_string (3)
